        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "INVISIBLE_SYSTEM",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Most people never see it. The strait is 31 km (17 nmi) long, with a width of 3,329 m at the northern entrance and 2,826 m at the southern entrance. Its maximum width is 3,420 m between Umuryeri and Büyükdere Limanı, and minimum width is 700 m between Kandilli Point and Aşiyan. The depth of the Bosporus varies from 13 to 110 m (43 to 361 ft) in midstream with an average of 65 m (213 ft). Ships over 150 metres long or 10 metres deep must pre-book their passage. In 2022 the dues levied by Turkey for freight ships increased 500% to US$4 per ton, the first change since 1983. The city of Istanbul's metropolitan population of 17 million inhabitants extends inland from both banks. Black Sea exports of grain, oil and metals depend on transit through the Bosporus.",
            "claims": [
              "C12",
              "C13",
              "C14",
              "C15",
              "C16",
              "C17",
              "C18"
            ],
            "role": "evidence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "WHERE_IT_EXISTS",
        "paragraphs": []
      },
      {
        "section": "HOW_IT_WORKS",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Here is how it works. Ships follow a winding 31 km channel through Istanbul, with long vessels pre-booking passage.",
            "claims": [
              "C2"
            ],
            "role": "evidence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "WHAT_DEPENDS_ON_IT",
        "paragraphs": []
      },
      {
        "section": "BOTTLENECK",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "That is the bottleneck. At its narrowest the strait is only 700 m wide, with sharp turns and heavy local ferry traffic.",
            "claims": [
              "C19"
            ],
            "role": "evidence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "WHY_THE_BOTTLENECK_EXISTS",
        "paragraphs": []
      },
      {
        "section": "FAILURE_SCENARIO",
        "paragraphs": []
      },
      {
        "section": "CASCADING_CONSEQUENCES",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "The failure would not stay contained. A grounding or collision can halt transits and queue ships at both ends.",
            "claims": [
